<workout_file>
	<author>Chris Murphy (via TrainingPeaks)</author>
	<name>Threshold Tolerance: 4x10M</name>
	<description>20M building up to 60-70% FTP to warm up, including 1M @ 100% FTP.

4x10M @ 98-102% FTP, taking 3M of easy spinning for active recovery between intervals (roughly 40-50% FTP, but coasting and light pedalling is fine too).

Remaining time up to 1H20M @ 60-70% FTP.

PURPOSE: Helps improve time to exhaustion at the lactate threshold, probably through improvements in improved pain tolerance, muscular endurance and possibly improved lactate shuttling and buffering.

This session might also contribute to increased lactate threshold power to a small extent, but it&apos;s main benefit is around increasing time to exhaustion, as evidenced here:
https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14740217/</description>
	<sportType>bike</sportType>
	<tags/>
	<workout>
		<SteadyState Duration="120" Power="0.5">
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="120" Power="0.6">
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="120" Power="0.7">
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="240" Power="0.65">
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="60" Power="1">
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="120" Power="0.65">
		</SteadyState>
		<IntervalsT Repeat="4" OnDuration="600" OnPower="1" OffDuration="180" OffPower="0.45">
		</IntervalsT>
		<Cooldown Duration="300" PowerHigh="0.55" PowerLow="0.75">
		</Cooldown>
	</workout>
</workout_file>